<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Panium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/200-bce">200 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-syrian-war">Fifth Syrian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Panium was fought around 200 BCE near the sources of the Jordan River during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifth-syrian-war">Fifth Syrian War</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> and the Ptolemaic army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scopas">Scopas</a>. Seleucid cavalry encircled and destroyed the Ptolemaic force. The victory gave the Seleucid Empire permanent control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coele-syria">Coele-Syria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-panium.jpg" alt="Battle of Panium" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: gugganij · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banias_Spring_Cliff_Pan%27s_Cave.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…both the potential and the limits of Seleucid power: the Fifth Syrian War (202–195 BCE), decided at the <b>Battle of Panium</b> around 200 BCE, where Antiochus's son Antiochus led the cavalry and elephants to rout the Ptolemaic army under the Aetolian general Scopas, permanently secured Coele-Syria; but the…</blockquote><a href="/empire/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
